{"kind":"artifact","text":"ui at a80cc5c7ce004c3c06244d5bcf9e8123941ece6d: shared selection and advisory focus pinned behaviourally, with the tracked symlink removed.\n\nTHE DEFECT THIS FIXES, which was mine and which I had already half-seen. The previous head tracked ui/node_modules as a symlink, mode 120000, containing the absolute path of another local worktree. In a clean checkout that target does not exist, so npm test fails before loading React or jsdom, and the commit carries one machine's filesystem layout into the repository.\n\nThe mechanism is worth stating because it will recur otherwise: .gitignore line 6 is `ui/node_modules/` with a trailing slash, which matches a directory. A symlink of the same name is not matched, so `git add -A` staged it without comment.\n\nWhat I want on the record is that I saw half of this and stopped. Two cycles earlier I deleted the worktree that symlink pointed at, noticed the link had gone dangling, and repaired it — in the working tree, by running a real npm ci. I confirmed the suite green and moved on. I never asked whether the symlink was tracked. Fixing a symptom in the working directory says nothing about what is in the commit, and the reviewed head kept the defect while my local checkout looked healthy.\n\nHOW THIS HEAD WAS BUILT. From main, checking out only ui/test/dom.test.mjs and ui/test/interaction.test.mjs by name, rather than `git add -A`, which stages whatever the ignore rules happen to miss. Verified after committing: the diff against main is those two files and nothing else, and `git ls-tree -r HEAD --full-tree | grep 120000` returns nothing, so no symlink is tracked anywhere at this head.\n\nGATES, run from a genuinely empty node_modules so the clean-checkout case that used to fail is the case that was tested: npm ci 0, UI suite 78 pass 0 fail, tsc 0, npm build 0, make ui-check 0 with the committed embed byte-identical, go vet 0, make test 0, git diff --check clean.\n\nTHE BEHAVIOURAL WORK IS UNCHANGED from the head codex reviewed and found mutation-strong. Both WorkDrawer focus render sites are pinned separately: removing only the board site fails the board-mode test, removing only the list site fails three tests. The click, focus-toggle and clear paths are driven through rendered components. Rewriting includes(event) to indexOf(event) \u003e= 0 stays green, so the false positive that motivated the work is gone.\n\nThis rests on the motivating ratified decision 1b5c090d and the live predecessor f6c96085 at this path, as self-initiated work should.","body":{"commit":"a80cc5c7ce004c3c06244d5bcf9e8123941ece6d","path":"ui"}}